 "title": "Square Glide Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the bouncy, gliding square-wave lead of 80s film and TV themes: a clean, hollow tone that slides between notes, with a dotted echo behind it.\n\nHow it's built: one oscillator's PULSE (a square), its pitch through a Slew for the glides; the Ladder filter with a little envelope for a soft 'blip' at the start of each note; a Delay. One voice.\n\nPlay: catchy, staccato melodies with octave jumps; play legato where you want a slide.\n\nTweak: the Slew's times, WIDTH (narrower is reedier), the delay's TIME (try a dotted eighth of your tempo), the filter envelope's DECAY.",
